  "passed": true,
  "reading": "a map, not a verdict. Support and drag both scale with the writing rate, so the physical question is what the orbit pays for a given amount of help: at a declared support fraction f, does the angular-momentum-change time exceed the time the track needs to build? The drag is set by the most recent passage and saturates immediately, while the support accumulates over the memory time, which is why long memory and wide tracks are the surviving direction"
 },
